  formulas: [
    { label: "Needn't have", structure: "Needn't have + V\u2083 (past unnecessary action)\nI needn't have brought an umbrella.", color: 'green' },
    { label: "Had better", structure: "Had better + V (strong advice)\nYou'd better see a doctor.", color: 'blue' },
    { label: 'Be supposed to', structure: "Be supposed to + V (expected/obliged)\nWe're supposed to be there at 8.", color: 'red' },
    { label: 'Dare', structure: "Dare + V (have courage)\nI daren't tell him the truth.", color: 'purple' },
  ],
  rules: [
    "1\uFE0F\u20E3 NEEDN'T HAVE VS DIDN'T NEED TO\n\nNeedn't have + V\u2083: qilganman, lekin kerak emas edi (I did it but it was unnecessary)\n  I needn't have bought so much food.\n  (I bought a lot, but it was unnecessary)\n\nDidn't need to + V: qilmaganman, chunki kerak emas edi (I didn't do it because it wasn't necessary)\n  I didn't need to buy any food.\n  (I didn't buy it because I had enough)\n\n\uD83D\uDD34 Farq:\n  Needn't have done = I did it (unnecessary)\n  Didn't need to do = I didn't do it (unnecessary)\n\n\uD83D\uDD34 Needn't have = regret or relief about a past action",
    "2\uFE0F\u20E3 NEEDN'T HAVE — BATAFSIL\n\nNeedn't have + past participle — o'tmishda qilingan, lekin keraksiz bo'lgan harakat:\n\n  I needn't have cooked so much. Nobody was hungry.\n  (I cooked a lot, but nobody ate it)\n\n  She needn't have worried. Everything was fine.\n  (She worried, but it was unnecessary)\n\n  We needn't have hurried. The train was late.\n  (We hurried, but the train was late)\n\n\uD83D\uDD34 Needn't have = 'It was not necessary, but I did it'\n\uD83D\uDD34 Often expresses relief: 'Oh good, I needn't have worried!'\n\uD83D\uDD34 Negative: needn't have = didn't need to (but different meaning)",
    "3\uFE0F\u20E3 DIDN'T NEED TO — BATAFSIL\n\nDidn't need to + V — o'tmishda kerak bo'lmagan, va odatda qilinmagan harakat:\n\n  I didn't need to wake up early. It was a holiday.\n  (I slept in)\n\n  She didn't need to pay. It was free.\n  (She didn't pay)\n\n  We didn't need to book a table. The restaurant was empty.\n  (We didn't book)\n\n\uD83D\uDD34 Didn't need to = 'It was not necessary, so I didn't do it'\n\uD83D\uDD34 But sometimes: 'I didn't need to buy tickets (because I already had them)' = I did it for a different reason",
    "4\uFE0F\u20E3 HAD BETTER\n\nHad better ('d better) — kuchli maslahat yoki ogohlantirish (agar qilmasang, yomon oqibatlar bo'ladi):\n\n  You'd better see a doctor.\n  (Agar bormasang, sog'lig'ing yomonlashishi mumkin)\n\n  I'd better finish this today.\n  (Agar tugatmasam, muammo bo'ladi)\n\n  We'd better not be late.\n  (Agar kechiksak, jazo bo'ladi)\n\n\uD83D\uDD34 Had better \u2260 Should:\n  Should = general advice\n  Had better = strong warning + negative consequence\n\n\uD83D\uDD34 Had better + base verb (no to)\n\uD83D\uDD34 Negative: had better NOT + V",
    "5\uFE0F\u20E3 BE SUPPOSED TO\n\nBe supposed to — kutilgan, rejalashtirilgan yoki majburiyat:\n\n  We're supposed to be there at 9 AM.\n  (We are expected to be there)\n\n  You're not supposed to park here.\n  (It is not allowed)\n\n  The train was supposed to arrive at 6.\n  (It was scheduled to arrive)\n\n  I was supposed to call her yesterday.\n  (I had an obligation)\n\n\uD83D\uDD34 Be supposed to = be expected to / be obligated to\n\uD83D\uDD34 Present: am/is/are supposed to\n\uD83D\uDD34 Past: was/were supposed to\n\uD83D\uDD34 Negative: be NOT supposed to = not allowed",
    "6\uFE0F\u20E3 DARE\n\nDare — jur'at qilmoq, tavakkal qilmoq. Modal va oddiy fe'l sifatida ishlatiladi:\n\nMODAL DARE (no 'to', no -s, mainly negative):\n  I daren't tell him.\n  Dare you ask her?\n  He dare not refuse.\n\nORDINARY VERB DARE (with 'to', -s):\n  He doesn't dare to tell her.\n  She dared to argue with the boss.\n  Nobody dares to complain.\n\nHOW DARE YOU! — kuchli norozilik:\n  How dare you speak to me like that!\n  How dare he say such a thing!\n\n\uD83D\uDD34 I dare say = ehtimol, menimcha:\n  I dare say you're right.\n\n\uD83D\uDD34 Modal dare ko'proq BrE, ordinary dare AmE va BrE.",
    "7\uFE0F\u20E3 O'ZBEKCHA XATOLAR\n\n\u2022 Needn't have va didn't need to ni adashtirish:\n  I needn't have bought it = I bought it (unnecessary)\n  I didn't need to buy it = I didn't buy it (unnecessary)\n\n\u2022 Had better ni odatdagi better bilan adashtirish:\n  XATO: You better go. \u2192 You'd BETTER go. (had better)\n  XATO: You had better to go \u2192 You had better go.\n\n\u2022 Be supposed to ni be suppose to deb yozish:\n  XATO: I'm suppose to \u2192 I'm supposed to\n\n\u2022 Dare ni noto'g'ri ishlatish:\n  XATO: I don't dare tell him. \u2192 I daren't tell him.\n  (Modal dare \u2192 daren't, daren't, dare not)",
  ],
