    id: 'contrastive-reading',
    title: 'Dual Economy: Traditional and Modern Sectors',
    passage: `Uzbekistan's economy presents a fascinating contrast between traditional and modern sectors. While agriculture still employs 27% of the workforce, its contribution to GDP has fallen to 25%. The services sector, on the other hand, has grown to 46% of GDP. Unlike many developing countries that rely heavily on natural resources, Uzbekistan has diversified into manufacturing and technology. However, the informal economy remains a challenge. Nevertheless, the government has made significant progress in formalising businesses through digital registration. In contrast to neighbouring countries, Uzbekistan's reform pace has been notably rapid.`,
